scope.reasoning:
The repro holds on 3.11.15 and 3.13.12. I extended it in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/1230efe6-3e44-5eb6-ad91-35910fea5db9/scratchpad/rt4/verify/check-metrics-smoke-masks-refusal/ext.py. On a result with "smoke": True, the G:exercises entry gets the bare note 'smoke run' for every GateSpecError, even when the trace is present. I confirmed this for NOT_EXERCISED, a swallowed NESTED_SECTION, STALE_TRACE and NO_TRACE; the non-smoke result gives the full [V5:...] text in each case.

Smoke is not what makes the entry unusable. On the same smoke result, a complete trace reads usable=True with note=None. So when usable=False appears with 'smoke run', the note wrongly blames the smoke flag, and the real reason (a missing target, a stale trace or a swallowed nesting refusal) is dropped.

The behavior contradicts three things:
- the spec sentence "reports usable: False with the refusal text";
- the code's own comment above the loop: "a harness that forgot a section learns it here, with the reason";
- the precedent of the v3 and v4 loops, which use the smoke note only for an absent path and report present-but-bad values with their real reason even on smoke.

No verdict is affected, so this is not a BLOCKER:
- usable stays False;
- score(smoke=True) never reads coverage;
- a full-run score() still refuses NOT_EXERCISED.

It is not a mere NOTE either, because the pre-run tool reports a false cause and loses the diagnostic. Repo harnesses do write "smoke": SMOKE into their results; papers/disjoint-worlds/run_b50.py and the frozen exam's own self-scoring (run_protocol_v5e.py around line 3650) both call check_metrics on smoke results and ignore unusable when SMOKE is set. So an author doing a smoke dry run sees 'smoke run', which looks like the expected "absent on smoke" note, and launches the full run. The coverage refusal then appears only after the compute is spent, which is exactly what check_metrics exists to prevent.

No stated limit, disclosed over-blocking or pinned residual covers this. Implementation and spec disagree, and the smallest honest fix is in the code, so I classify it as a DEFECT (false message) rather than SPEC_FALSE.

Not a finding for EXAM_HOLE: the fix variant passes the frozen exam, and the frozen exam does not pin either behavior.
